    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on speed-centric upside, anchored by our strongest play of the day, **Mickey Moniak** (75.33). **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a highly favorable platoon matchup against Logan Webb, providing the ideal ceiling for our outfield. Following closely is **Brice Turang** (73.74) and **James Wood** (73.57). **Brice Turang**\u2019s efficiency is driven by a strong matchup against J. Cabrera, while **James Wood** remains a must-start despite the presence of a tough catcher behind the plate; his elite xwOBA (0.418) and leadoff spot make him an offensive engine. We are also monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** (61.80) and **Jose Caballero** (60.52), as both leverage their sprint speed against pitchers with slower deliveries, keeping them in our active lineup despite marginal platoon constraints.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was the exclusion of **Kyle Karros** (46.00) and **Josh Naylor** (45.59). **Kyle Karros** was the closest to cracking the lineup, as he received a significant park boost in his clash with Webb; however, his lower base projection compared to our middle infield depth made him the odd man out. **Josh Naylor** remains benched primarily due to the severe SP skill penalty associated with facing Cease, which drags his efficiency below our 40.0 floor. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno** (43.72) and **Corbin Carroll** (52.12), both of whom are facing the formidable Harrison; while **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s speed is a constant variable, the SP skill drop-off from the matchup risk is substantial enough to temper expectations. We are also keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing** (52.53) and **Edwin Arroyo** (50.06), as their bottom-third lineup positions dampen their otherwise promising matchups against King and Rogers, respectively.",
